+++ b/docs/api.rst
@@ -442,6 +442,20 @@ own loader, subclass :class:`BaseLoader` and override `get_source`.
 
 Here a list of the builtin loaders Jinja provides:
 
+``FileSystemLoader`` can cache successful path resolution.
+``path_cache_size`` defaults to zero, disabling caching.
+Positive integers bound least-recently-used eviction.
+Booleans and negative values are rejected. Misses are not
+cached. Missing files and earlier matching search paths
+cause resolution again. The cache stores filenames, not
+source, and does not replace the compiled-template cache.
+
+Use ``clear_path_cache()`` to remove entries, or
+``resize_path_cache(capacity)`` to change the bound immediately.
+Resizing to zero clears and disables caching. Subclasses may override
+``resolve_template_path(template)`` for uncached lookup. It returns a
+filename or ``None`` and is not called for valid cache hits.
+
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.FileSystemLoader
 
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.PackageLoader
@@ -920,3 +934,5 @@ returned by the :meth:`Environment.parse` method.
 .. autofunction:: jinja2.meta.find_undeclared_variables
 
 .. autofunction:: jinja2.meta.find_referenced_templates
+
+Cached sources ignore configured encoding and never go stale.
